[
    {
        "content": "<p>In the following situation:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Julia\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c\">#-------------------------------------</span>\n<span class=\"k\">module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Internal</span>\n<span class=\"k\">struct</span> <span class=\"kt\">WrongInput</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Exception</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">end</span>\n<span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">_</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">throw</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">WrongInput</span><span class=\"p\">())</span>\n<span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">::</span><span class=\"kt\">Int</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n<span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"k\">export</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n<span class=\"k\">end</span>\n\n<span class=\"c\">#-------------------------------------</span>\n<span class=\"k\">module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Exposed</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">..</span><span class=\"n\">Internal</span>\n<span class=\"k\">struct</span> <span class=\"kt\">NiceReport</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Exception</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">end</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">welcome</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">try</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">catch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">isa</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Internal</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">WrongInput</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&amp;&amp;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rethrow</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">NiceReport</span><span class=\"p\">())</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">rethrow</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">end</span>\n<span class=\"k\">export</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">welcome</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">Base</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">showerror</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">io</span><span class=\"o\">::</span><span class=\"kt\">IO</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">::</span><span class=\"kt\">NiceReport</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">io</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"Don't worry it's not that bad just try again &lt;3\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">end</span>\n\n<span class=\"c\">#-------------------------------------</span>\n<span class=\"c\"># User.</span>\n<span class=\"k\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Exposed</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">my_u</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">welcome</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">my_v</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">my_u</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">my_w</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">my_v</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">my_w</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"hi\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>User obtains the following stacktrace:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Text only\"><pre><span></span><code>ERROR: LoadError: Don't worry it's not that bad just try again &lt;3\nStacktrace:\n  [1] f(::String)                   &lt;&lt;\n    @ Main.Internal ./test.jl.jl:4  &lt;&lt;\n  [2] g(x::String)                  &lt;&lt;\n    @ Main.Internal ./test.jl.jl:6  &lt;&lt;\n  [3] h(x::String)                  &lt;&lt;\n    @ Main.Internal ./test.jl.jl:7  &lt;&lt;  Garbage (from user POV).\n  [4] p(x::String)                  &lt;&lt;  Useless for debugging: not a bug (in the lib).\n    @ Main.Exposed ./test.jl.jl:17  &lt;&lt;\n  [5] q(x::String)                  &lt;&lt;\n    @ Main.Exposed ./test.jl.jl:18  &lt;&lt;\n  [6] welcome(x::String)            &lt;&lt;\n    @ Main.Exposed ./test.jl.jl:21  &lt;&lt;\n  [7] my_u(x::String)            &lt;&lt;\n    @ Main ./test.jl.jl:37       &lt;&lt;\n  [8] my_v(x::String)            &lt;&lt;\n    @ Main ./test.jl.jl:38       &lt;&lt;   *USEFUL* (from user POV).\n  [9] my_w(x::String)            &lt;&lt;\n    @ Main ./test.jl.jl:39       &lt;&lt;\n [10] top-level scope            &lt;&lt;\n    @ ./test.jl.jl:41            &lt;&lt;\n [11] top-level scope            &lt;&lt;\n    @ REPL[1]:1                  &lt;&lt;\nin expression starting at ./test.jl:41\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Is there a way I could reliably trim frames <code>[1]</code> to <code>[6]</code> so as not to bury them into the lib implementation detail? The relevant info for them only starts on frame <code>[7]</code>, and the deepest the lib the further <em>up</em> they need to scroll so as to just <em>read</em> the report.</p>",
        "id": 613806373,
        "sender_full_name": "iago-lito",
        "timestamp": 1785484240
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Using <code>throw(NiceReport())</code> instead of <code>rethrow(NiceReport())</code> does cut it exactly where it should, but then the <code>caused by</code> section still flushes the report up.</p>",
        "id": 613806538,
        "sender_full_name": "iago-lito",
        "timestamp": 1785484325
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><em>(currently investigating <a href=\"https://docs.julialang.org/en/v1/base/base/#Base.current_exceptions\"><code>Base.current_exceptions</code></a>)</em></p>",
        "id": 613806834,
        "sender_full_name": "iago-lito",
        "timestamp": 1785484478
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><em>(nah, it doesn't seem we can mutate the returned <code>ExceptionStack</code>, can we?)</em></p>",
        "id": 613807497,
        "sender_full_name": "iago-lito",
        "timestamp": 1785484773
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't think so, but also, I think it's a bad idea to even try. A stack trace should contain the entire call stack so it's maximally usable for debuggning. Once you try messing with it to improve user friendliness, you should not be throwing un-caught exceptions, but instead print an error to stderr or something like that</p>",
        "id": 613807554,
        "sender_full_name": "Jakob Nybo Andersen",
        "timestamp": 1785484792
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Just printint to stderr would drop frames <code>[7]</code> to <code>[11]</code> which <em>are</em> useful to user IMO.</p>",
        "id": 613807898,
        "sender_full_name": "iago-lito",
        "timestamp": 1785484868
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Also the purpose of <code>rethrow(e)</code> in case of unexpected exception is to really obtain the full stacktrace in case the <em>lib</em> itself needs debugging, so I wouldn't worry about this?</p>",
        "id": 613808062,
        "sender_full_name": "iago-lito",
        "timestamp": 1785484921
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It's going to be difficult to determine beforehand what's useful to a user. What's to say the error isn't truly caused by something internal in your library?</p>",
        "id": 613808097,
        "sender_full_name": "Jakob Nybo Andersen",
        "timestamp": 1785484937
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>When I say difficult, I mean that it's not possible at all. You can't have that information</p>",
        "id": 613808162,
        "sender_full_name": "Jakob Nybo Andersen",
        "timestamp": 1785484963
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This pattern does (IMO):</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Julia\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">try</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"k\">catch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">isa</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ExpectedExceptionType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">||</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rethrow</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c\"># Obtain full stracktrace for debugging.</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c\"># or handle e gracefully, forgetting about internal detail.</span>\n<span class=\"k\">end</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 613808246,
        "sender_full_name": "iago-lito",
        "timestamp": 1785484992
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ahh so you'd want something like Python's <code>raise X from None</code>. Yeah that makes sense</p>",
        "id": 613808382,
        "sender_full_name": "Jakob Nybo Andersen",
        "timestamp": 1785485040
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Don't know that one, but yeah why not :)</p>",
        "id": 613808442,
        "sender_full_name": "iago-lito",
        "timestamp": 1785485060
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I wish to trim whichever part of the stack collected <em>before</em> the point I can assert that detail doesn't matter.</p>",
        "id": 613808664,
        "sender_full_name": "iago-lito",
        "timestamp": 1785485137
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(and I take responsibility for this as the lib author ofc)</p>",
        "id": 613808700,
        "sender_full_name": "iago-lito",
        "timestamp": 1785485145
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah yeah I see. I don't think that exists. But it would be nice to have</p>",
        "id": 613809379,
        "sender_full_name": "Jakob Nybo Andersen",
        "timestamp": 1785485373
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Siigh, should I request it you think or is there already relevant momentum in that direction?</p>",
        "id": 613809616,
        "sender_full_name": "iago-lito",
        "timestamp": 1785485456
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think Julia's errors have gotten very little attention in general</p>",
        "id": 613811239,
        "sender_full_name": "Jakob Nybo Andersen",
        "timestamp": 1785486047
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Alright. I'll report as a feat request unless someone else teaches us something about this today :)</p>",
        "id": 613811478,
        "sender_full_name": "iago-lito",
        "timestamp": 1785486140
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>(re)throw(e; afresh=true)</code> or sth would be nice.</p>",
        "id": 613811987,
        "sender_full_name": "iago-lito",
        "timestamp": 1785486353
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'd really like a way to trim out noise from stacktraces too. The context I have this from is writing code like this:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Julia\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">macro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">outline</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"o\">...</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">fargs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">esc</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"k\">end</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">])</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">body</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">args</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"k\">end</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nd\">@gensym</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">quote</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"o\">$</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">$</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fargs</span><span class=\"o\">...</span><span class=\"p\">),)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">$</span><span class=\"n\">body</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"nd\">@noinline</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">$</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">$</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fargs</span><span class=\"o\">...</span><span class=\"p\">),)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">end</span>\n<span class=\"k\">end</span>\n\n<span class=\"k\">function</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">my_sqrt</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n<span class=\"w\">          </span><span class=\"nd\">@outline</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">throw</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">ArgumentError</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"my_sqrt does not take negative arguments, got </span><span class=\"si\">$x</span><span class=\"s\">\"</span><span class=\"p\">))</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">end</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"o\">...</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>\n<span class=\"k\">end</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Here <code>@outline</code> automates the process of making a function barrier for me so that the error-path doesn't clog up the generated code for <code>my_sqrt</code>, which helps optimization, and then the value can be used in the error message without worrying about all the involved io/string operations.</p>\n<p>But the downside is that it clogs up stacktraces with irrelevant information.</p>",
        "id": 613880972,
        "sender_full_name": "Mason Protter",
        "timestamp": 1785510593
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/JuliaLang/julia/issues/62594\">https://github.com/JuliaLang/julia/issues/62594</a>.. let's see ¯\\_(ツ)_/¯</p>",
